              "language": "en",
              "description": "JGI publishes all its sequenced genomes on its Genome Portal. Here you can download sequence files, BLAST against a particular genome, and view annotations. Advanced tools, including genome, GO, KEGG, and KOG browsers, are available for eukaryotes. JGI''s Genome Browser lets you browse through JGI-predicted genes, view sequences, and study detailed alignments with nucleotide and amino acid sequences from relevant sequence databases. Individual genomes sites can be reached using the Tree of Life. These sites provide download access to sequence files and tools for annotation and BLAST alignment. Eukaryotic genome sites include additional resources such as genome browsing, search, and functional (KEG/KOGG/GO) annotations.",
